      "writtenOn": "2022-05-28T16:59:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m less than enthusiast about the approach of this patch. Since multiqueue support has been defined in the UFSHCI 4.0 standard and since all multiqueue implementations are expected to implement that standard, I\u0027d prefer a single implementation of MCQ in the UFS driver core. This patch forces each UFS controller vendor to implement MCQ support in the UFS host driver instead of in the UFS core.",
      "revId": "de145832c1cd45d315fbe71e32accdc54819001f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8dd10314_5d823809",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-02T18:27:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is too complex as an ANDROID patch. Since the upstream changes for MCQ will not land in time, please refactor this using vendor hooks and ANDROID_VENDOR_DATA.\n\nPlease split into 2 patches:\n1) KMI breaking changes to ufshcd-pltfrm.h (add ANDROID_VENDOR_DATA)\n2) Remaining changes (adding hook implementation -- see suggestions in comments)",
      "revId": "de145832c1cd45d315fbe71e32accdc54819001f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
